<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN"
  "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <!--
      Merged into the generated Info.plist by the Tauri macOS bundler.

      System-audio capture (macos-audio PRD §4.6, §8.6). The Core Audio Process Tap path
      (macOS 14.2+) triggers the "System Audio Recording Only" TCC prompt, which requires this
      usage string. The ScreenCaptureKit fallback (13.0+) rides the existing Screen Recording
      permission and needs no extra key here. On the 10.15 floor neither backend runs, so the
      key is simply unused. Confirm the exact prompt/entitlement on real 14.2 hardware
      (AUDIO_NOTES_MACOS.md §4.6).
    -->
    <key>NSAudioCaptureUsageDescription</key>
    <string>ScreenExtend streams this Mac's audio output to devices you connect, when you enable System Audio for a device.</string>

    <!--
      App Transport Security. In `tauri dev` the WKWebView loads the Vite dev server over plain
      HTTP (devUrl http://localhost:1420). macOS 10.15 (Catalina) enforces ATS strictly and refuses
      that load, so the whole UI comes up blank with "The resource could not be loaded because the
      App Transport Security policy requires the use of a secure connection." Newer macOS is lenient
      about loopback, which is why this only bites on the 10.15 floor.

        - NSAllowsLocalNetworking exempts loopback / .local hosts (the dev server) from ATS.
        - NSAllowsArbitraryLoadsInWebContent lets the WKWebView load plain-HTTP content while ATS
          stays fully enforced for the rest of the app (NSURLSession, etc.). Scoped to web content
          only — it does not disable ATS globally.

      In a production build the frontend is served from the bundled `tauri://localhost` custom
      scheme, which is not subject to ATS, so both keys are inert there (they only matter for dev).
    -->
    <key>NSAppTransportSecurity</key>
    <dict>
        <key>NSAllowsLocalNetworking</key>
        <true/>
        <key>NSAllowsArbitraryLoadsInWebContent</key>
        <true/>
    </dict>
</dict>
</plist>
